<speak>That would help. Sometimes I over-explain because I don't want to seem difficult. I start describing the warehouse meeting, then a supplier visit, then something at my daughter's school, and by the end even I can't remember which afternoon is free. Better to give a few suitable windows. Also, if I miss a call, please don't assume I'm avoiding it. I may be somewhere noisy, or I've left the phone in my bag while I'm speaking to someone. A short message is usually easier to notice afterwards.</speak>